SELECT $bmsq$Case study: how a real estate firm got leads in 30 days$bmsq$, $bmsq$real-estate-leads-30-days-case-study$bmsq$, $bmsq$Case study template: how a real estate firm set up ads, WhatsApp follow-up and lead scoring in its first 30 days, with verified results from the account.$bmsq$, $bmsq$Case study template: how a real estate firm set up ads, WhatsApp follow-up and lead scoring in its first 30 days, with verified results from the account.$bmsq$, $bmsq$<p>In 30 days, [EDITOR: client name or anonymous descriptor] went from [EDITOR: starting position, e.g. "no active campaigns" or "portal leads only"] to [EDITOR: verified number] qualified leads and [EDITOR: verified number] site visits by running a single-project offer from its own ad accounts and replying to every enquiry instantly on WhatsApp. Below is exactly what was set up, week by week, and what the numbers showed.</p><p><strong>[EDITOR: this post is a case-study TEMPLATE. Do not publish until every [EDITOR] placeholder is replaced with verified figures from the ad account and CRM, and the client has given written permission to be named or quoted. If permission is not given, describe the client anonymously, e.g. "a mid-size developer in Bengaluru".]</strong></p><h2>Client snapshot</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Client</td><td>[EDITOR: name with written permission, or anonymous descriptor]</td></tr><tr><td>City and market</td><td>[EDITOR]</td></tr><tr><td>Project type</td><td>[EDITOR: e.g. 2 and 3BHK apartments, under construction]</td></tr><tr><td>Sales team size</td><td>[EDITOR]</td></tr><tr><td>Previous lead sources</td><td>[EDITOR]</td></tr><tr><td>Period covered</td><td>[EDITOR: exact start and end dates]</td></tr><tr><td>Ad spend in period</td><td>[EDITOR: from ad account billing]</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>The challenge</h2><p>[EDITOR: describe the client's real problem in two or three sentences, in their words if possible. Examples of the kind of thing to write: leads arriving but going cold before anyone called, portal leads shared with competitors, no way to tell which ads produced site visits.]</p><h2>The goal for the first 30 days</h2><p>[EDITOR: the specific goal agreed with the client at the start, e.g. a target number of qualified leads or site visits, or simply "set up a measurable pipeline". Use the goal as it was actually written at the time.]</p><h2>What we set up</h2><p>[EDITOR: confirm each step below matches what was actually done for this client and delete anything that was not.]</p><h3>Week 1: offer, tracking and approval</h3><ul><li>Agreed one clear project offer with configuration, price range and location benefits.</li><li>Checked RERA details were shown correctly in ads.</li><li>Connected tracking and the CRM so every lead's source was recorded.</li><li>Built campaigns in the client's own ad accounts, staged paused, and walked the client through them for approval.</li></ul><h3>Week 2: launch and instant follow-up</h3><ul><li>Launched approved campaigns on [EDITOR: platforms actually used].</li><li>The Follow-up AI replied to each new enquiry on WhatsApp the moment the lead responded, asking about configuration, budget and timeline.</li><li>Leads were scored and pushed into the CRM so the sales team called the warmest first.</li></ul><h3>Week 3: optimise</h3><ul><li>The optimisation loop reviewed campaigns every 20 minutes, moving budget toward ads producing qualified leads.</li><li>[EDITOR: one or two specific changes made this week and why, from the change log.]</li></ul><h3>Week 4: site visits and review</h3><ul><li>Site visit slots offered on WhatsApp with reminders the day before.</li><li>Weekly plain-English reports shared with the client.</li><li>[EDITOR: what was reviewed at the end of the month and what was decided.]</li></ul><h2>How the numbers in this case study are measured</h2><p>So readers can compare fairly, here is what each term means in this post. A <strong>lead</strong> is any form submission or WhatsApp conversation started from a campaign. A <strong>qualified lead</strong> is a lead whose budget, configuration and timeline matched the project, based on their answers. A <strong>site visit completed</strong> is a visit recorded by the sales team in the CRM. <strong>Cost per qualified lead</strong> is total ad spend in the period divided by qualified leads. [EDITOR: confirm these definitions match how the client's CRM recorded each stage, and adjust if not.]</p><h2>Results</h2><p>[EDITOR: every number here must come from the ad account and CRM exports for the exact period above. Keep the screenshots on file.]</p><table><thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Before (if known)</th><th>First 30 days</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Total leads</td><td>[EDITOR]</td><td>[EDITOR]</td><td>[EDITOR: ad account / CRM]</td></tr><tr><td>Qualified leads</td><td>[EDITOR]</td><td>[EDITOR]</td><td>[EDITOR]</td></tr><tr><td>Median first-response time</td><td>[EDITOR]</td><td>[EDITOR]</td><td>[EDITOR]</td></tr><tr><td>Site visits booked</td><td>[EDITOR]</td><td>[EDITOR]</td><td>[EDITOR]</td></tr><tr><td>Site visits completed</td><td>[EDITOR]</td><td>[EDITOR]</td><td>[EDITOR]</td></tr><tr><td>Bookings (if any in period)</td><td>[EDITOR]</td><td>[EDITOR]</td><td>[EDITOR]</td></tr><tr><td>Cost per qualified lead</td><td>[EDITOR]</td><td>[EDITOR]</td><td>[EDITOR]</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>[EDITOR: add one real example and screenshot here — client name only with written permission]</strong></p><h2>In the client's words</h2><p>[EDITOR: a short quote from the client, approved in writing, word for word. If no approved quote exists, delete this section.]</p><h2>What we learned</h2><p>[EDITOR: two or three honest lessons from this account. Include at least one thing that did not work. Readers trust case studies that admit what went wrong.]</p><h2>What would change in month two</h2><p>[EDITOR: next steps actually planned, e.g. new creative, NRI campaign, adjusting the qualifying question.]</p><h2>Context: results vary</h2><p>This is one firm's experience over one period. Results depend on the project, location, price, market conditions, offer and the sales team's follow-up. We do not guarantee results. For the full method we use with property clients, read the <a href="/blog/real-estate-lead-generation-playbook">real estate lead generation playbook</a>. For the WhatsApp side, see the <a href="/blog/click-to-whatsapp-ads-setup-guide">click-to-WhatsApp setup guide</a>. You can also learn more on our <a href="/industries/real-estate">real estate page</a>.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Can every real estate project expect similar results in 30 days?</h3><p>No. Thirty days is enough to set up, launch and learn, but results depend heavily on the project, pricing, location and market. Treat this as an example of the process, not a promise.</p><h3>Did the ads run in the client's own account?</h3><p>Yes. BoostMySites runs campaigns in the client's own ad accounts and billing, and campaigns stay paused until the client approves them. [EDITOR: confirm for this client.]</p><h3>What did the client need to provide?</h3><p>Project details, approved pricing, RERA information, creative assets such as photos and walkthroughs, and a sales contact to take over qualified leads. [EDITOR: adjust to what this client actually provided.]</p><p>Want to plan the first 30 days for your own project? <a href="/#contact-form">Get my client acquisition plan</a>.</p>$bmsq$, $bmsq${"name": "Kavya Shree.R", "avatar": "https://www.boostmysites.com/team/kavya.jpg", "bio": "Kavya Shree.R is Chief Marketing Officer at BoostMySites and runs the blog's content calendar. She writes about getting clients with ads, WhatsApp and follow-up systems for growing businesses."}$bmsq$::jsonb, '2026-11-25T03:30:00.000Z', 5, ARRAY[$bmsq$Proof$bmsq$,$bmsq$Real estate$bmsq$,$bmsq$Case study$bmsq$]::text[], 'https://www.boostmysites.com/brand/hero-poster.jpg', $bmsq$Proof$bm